//? Title: SlowFast:two complete pathways and visible tensor Adam
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Action recognition must combine appearance and temporal variation in actual video. Two complete R50 pathways process sparse and dense observations;the report exposes all tensor optimizer updates,zero residual gates and direct Fast-to-Slow interventions on original KTH clips.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.10_3d_and_video_convolutions/slowfast.cpp`.

> The method

The Slow path receives endpoint-inclusive sparse observations;the Fast path retains every selected observation with1/8the channels. Four learned temporal projections carry Fast features into Slow by channel concatenation. Both paths retain sixteen bottlenecks. For a residual branch y=ReLU(skip+gamma*BN(conv)+beta),gamma0 initializes an identity/projection route while gamma and beta can open the branch during fitting.

$$ L=-\frac1B\sum_{i=1}^{B}\log\operatorname{softmax}(z_i)_{y_i}. $$
\alttext(Mean categorical negative log likelihood over the current fitting batch.)

The visible Adam loop optimizes every learned leaf;moving BN arrays are updated by fitting forwards and restored with the matching learned checkpoint. Compact execution and the analytical full-reference census are labelled separately.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/slowfast_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/slowfast_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/slowfast_concept.tikz > build/slowfast_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/slowfast_concept.svg build/slowfast_concept.dvi > build/slowfast_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
