> Annotated confusion counts

The following program replots the complete frozen evaluation counts printed in the
predictor tables above. It reproduces those recorded measurements without refitting
or re-evaluating the model. `ConfusionMatrix::from_counts` owns the integer tensor
counts and `save_svg` labels every cell. True class zero is the **top** row and
predicted class zero the left column. Counts are exact; colors use the observed
count range. Source class meanings remain those declared for the dataset above.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/slowfast_confusion_api_0.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  {
    const auto counts =
        n::from_vector(std::vector<std::int64_t>{0, 0, 2, 0, 0, 2, 0, 0, 2}, {3, 3});
    const auto matrix = n::ConfusionMatrix::from_counts(counts);
    if (std::abs(matrix.accuracy() - 0.333333) > 1e-5)
      return 1;
    matrix.save_svg(
        "build/slowfast_confusion_api_0.svg",
        {.title = "slowfast / learned SlowFast / 1", .cell_size = 52, .font_size = 13});
    std::print("Recorded evaluation 1: 6 observations; accuracy {:.6f}.\n", matrix.accuracy());
  }
}
```
